# Project Overview & Development Guide

This document provides a high-level overview of the `xsoulspace.github.io` project, its architecture, and the guiding principles for its development. It is intended to be a starting point for any developer or AI agent working on the codebase.

## 1. Core Idea & Vision

This project is the official portfolio website for **xsoulspace.dev**, an indie one-man project focused on creating excellent products through quality, iteration, and open-source principles. The website serves to showcase the project's work across several categories: Apps, Games, Utilities, and foundational open-source libraries.

The design philosophy, as outlined in `docs/plan_v2.md`, emphasizes a simple yet epic and unique user experience with distinct, purpose-driven layouts for each section.

## 2. Technology Stack

The project is built on a modern Vue.js 3 ecosystem:

- **Framework:** [Vue 3](https://vuejs.org/) (Composition API)
- **Build Tool:** [Vite](https://vitejs.dev/)
- **Language:** [TypeScript](https://www.typescriptlang.org/)
- **Routing:** [Vue Router 4](https://router.vuejs.org/)
- **Internationalization (i18n):** [Vue I18n](https://vue-i18n.intlify.dev/)
- **SEO & Meta Management:** [VueUse Head](https://vueuse.org/integrations/head/)
- **Styling:** Global CSS variables (`src/assets/main.css`) and scoped styles. [SASS](https://sass-lang.com/) is available.
- **Data Parsing:** [YAML](https://yaml.org/) for parsing content files.
- **Markdown Parsing:** [markdown-it](https://github.com/markdown-it/markdown-it) for rendering markdown content.

## 3. Project Architecture

The codebase is organized in a standard, scalable structure within the `src/` directory.

- **`main.ts`**: The application entry point. Initializes Vue, Router, and i18n.
- **`App.vue`**: The root Vue component, responsible for initializing the locale on startup.
- **`assets/`**: Contains global styles (`main.css`), static images, icons, and fonts.
- **`components/`**: Shared Vue components, organized by layout (`layout/`), page sections (`sections/`), and general UI elements (`ui/`), including the `LocaleSwitcher.vue`.
- **`composables/`**: Reusable Vue Composition API functions, including `useSEO.ts` and the new `useLocale.ts` for global language management.
- **`data/`**: Holds localized content in language-specific subdirectories (e.g., `data/en/`). This includes `.yaml` files for structured data and `.md` files for block content like the ethics letter.
- **`locales/`**: Contains translation files for static UI strings (`en.ts`, `ru.ts`).
- **`pages/`**: Top-level components that correspond to application routes.
- **`router/`**: Defines the application's routes in `index.ts`.
- **`services/`**: Contains business logic, such as the dynamic, locale-aware `projectService.ts`.
- **`types/`**: TypeScript type definitions for data models (`project.ts`).

### Rendering Flow

1.  The app is mounted in `main.ts`. `App.vue` then initializes the locale using the `useLocale` composable, checking `localStorage` or the browser's language.
2.  `App.vue` renders `AppLayout.vue`.
3.  `AppLayout.vue` provides the global structure, a persistent `<LocaleSwitcher />`, and a `<router-view>` outlet.
4.  Vue Router dynamically renders the appropriate page component from `src/pages/` inside the `<router-view>`.
5.  Page components are reactive to locale changes, automatically re-fetching their content via a `watch` effect when the user switches the language.

## 4. Guiding Principles & Implementation Plans

This section summarizes the development plan derived from `docs/plan_v2.md`.

### Main Page (`Index.vue`)

- **Layout:** A full-width, multi-row layout. Each row is a large, clickable link to a main section.
- **Component:** `src/components/sections/HomeNavigation.vue`.

### Project Showcase Pages (`Apps.vue`, `Games.vue`, `Utilities.vue`)

- **Layout:** A two-column design utilizing a **CSS Scroll Snap** pattern.
- **Component:** `src/pages/ProjectShowcasePage.vue` is the reusable template for these pages.

### Foundation Page (`Foundation.vue`)

- **Layout:** A two-column layout tailored for developers, with a package list and a code/description view.

### Ethics Page (`Ethics.vue`)

- **Layout:** A two-part page.
- **Part 1:** A **Bento Grid** to visually represent the studio's core principles.
- **Part 2:** A letter explaining the philosophy, loaded from a localized markdown file.
